usage: ./programs [-h] [--debug] [--no-build]
                  {list,help,run,build,cli,execute,bake,doctor,menu} ...

Discover, build and operate the local programs without writing driver code.

positional arguments:
  {list,help,run,build,cli,execute,bake,doctor,menu}
    list                search programs without building or running them
    help                read a program's usage without executing it
    run                 run one named program
    build               build one named program
    cli                 open the main CLI or pass it arguments
    execute             run a saved static membrane, IMASM or glyph file
    bake                bake a static membrane from ordinary inputs
    doctor              check local build tools and target availability
    menu                choose a program and enter its arguments interactively

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --debug               use a debug build instead of release
  --no-build            reuse existing Rust tools; bake recipes still compile
                        their outputs

Start with list, help PROGRAM, bake --help, or menu. No program runs when no
command is supplied.
